- Yeah.

780
00:25:05,136 --> 00:25:06,137
- Here comes the answer.

781
00:25:06,137 --> 00:25:07,472
- Let me check it out here.

782
00:25:07,472 --> 00:25:08,974
- What's it say, Crow?

783
00:25:08,974 --> 00:25:10,742
- I haven't quite figured
out how to read it yet.

784
00:25:10,742 --> 00:25:12,711
- You guys, it's kinda messy.

785
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:15,046
- Oh, well I guess are
computers are bug proof, huh?

786
00:25:15,046 --> 00:25:16,348
Well I'd like to be
on the mailing list

787
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,182
for one of those.

788
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:18,350
Sign me up.

789
00:25:19,951 --> 00:25:21,887
Well, its starting
to pile up here.

790
00:25:21,887 --> 00:25:22,821
- Yeah.

791
00:25:22,821 --> 00:25:23,655
So.

792
00:25:25,457 --> 00:25:27,325
We thought you'd
be happy for us.

793
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:30,128
- No, it's.

794
00:25:30,128 --> 00:25:32,130
- Can you see if it's
commercial sign yet, Crow?

795
00:25:32,130 --> 00:25:33,832
- I think we got
commercial sign, you guys.

796
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:36,201
Yeah, it's really neat.

797
00:25:37,269 --> 00:25:39,838
(upbeat music)

798
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:48,413
- [Servo] Sorry about
the mess there, Joel.

799
00:25:48,413 --> 00:25:49,347
- [Joel] That's okay.

800
00:25:49,347 --> 00:25:50,148
- We'll clean it up later.

801
00:25:50,148 --> 00:25:51,383
- [Joel] All right.

802
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:53,885
(tense music)

803
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:56,888
- Unit three, calling Urania.

804
00:25:56,888 --> 00:25:58,690
Have Cosmostraiter
on our radar screen.

805
00:25:58,690 --> 00:25:59,591
Appearance normal.

806
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:02,327
- Well, feeling all right?

807
00:26:02,327 --> 00:26:04,296
- [Joel] Not feeling
too good ourselves.

808
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:07,666
- Right in the clouds.

809
00:26:08,833 --> 00:26:10,602
- I'll be fine as soon
as I scrape my butt

810
00:26:10,602 --> 00:26:11,436
off the ceiling.

811
00:26:11,436 --> 00:26:13,238
- Someway behind us.

812
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:15,273
- I'm gonna loosen this belt.

813
00:26:15,273 --> 00:26:16,241
It's uncomfortable.

814
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:19,611
(mock grunting)

815
00:26:19,611 --> 00:26:20,779
- Hey, be careful, don't forget.

816
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:21,613
There's no gravity.

817
00:26:21,613 --> 00:26:22,781
We're in free fall now.

818
00:26:22,781 --> 00:26:23,848
- [Joel] No gravity?

819
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:27,419
(mock laughter)

820
00:26:28,887 --> 00:26:29,721
- I love to laugh.

821
00:26:29,721 --> 00:26:31,423
Long and loud and clear.

822
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:34,192
(goofy laughter)

823
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:39,931
- [Joel] Oh, even I
gotta laugh at that.

824
00:26:42,467 --> 00:26:44,035
- Nice trust, buddy.

825
00:26:44,035 --> 00:26:46,638
(all laughing)

826
00:26:50,208 --> 00:26:52,510
- [Servo] Wendy, Michael,
John, we can fly.

827
00:26:52,510 --> 00:26:53,678
- Gravity field, will you?

828
00:26:53,678 --> 00:26:55,914
(laughing)

829
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:58,883
- [Joel] Oh, that's rich.

830
00:26:58,883 --> 00:26:59,918
Oh.

831
00:26:59,918 --> 00:27:00,719
- Be careful.

832
00:27:00,719 --> 00:27:02,420
Not pushing the button.

833
00:27:02,420 --> 00:27:03,355
- Hey, you're pushing 50.

834
00:27:03,355 --> 00:27:04,756
You better get down here.

835
00:27:04,756 --> 00:27:07,258
(all laughing)

836
00:27:07,258 --> 00:27:08,326
- [Joel] Oh, let him go.

837
00:27:08,326 --> 00:27:10,929
(all laughing)

838
00:27:12,197 --> 00:27:13,331
- [Servo] The
laugh meter's high.

839
00:27:13,331 --> 00:27:15,900
(all laughing)

840
00:27:15,900 --> 00:27:17,235
- [Joel] Oh fun.

841
00:27:18,403 --> 00:27:21,206
Oh, Steve, your shin
bone is sticking out.

842
00:27:21,206 --> 00:27:22,240
- That was a dirty trick.

843
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,509
(mock laughter)

844
00:27:24,509 --> 00:27:25,944
- [Joel] Well, our first report

845
00:27:25,944 --> 00:27:28,480
says there's lot of good nature
ribbing going on up there.

846
00:27:29,714 --> 00:27:30,982
- This is Luna Three.

847
00:27:30,982 --> 00:27:33,451
We are receiving you well.

848
00:27:33,451 --> 00:27:34,719
Over and out.

849
00:27:34,719 --> 00:27:37,088
- Hello, Luna Three, we
hear you loud and clear.

850
00:27:37,088 --> 00:27:39,124
- [Servo] How are
we coming in, over?

851
00:27:40,125 --> 00:27:41,559
- Plus five.

852
00:27:41,559 --> 00:27:43,294
Course normal, course normal.

853
00:27:43,294 --> 00:27:45,764
- Our course is exactly
hyperbolic, no deviations.

854
00:27:45,764 --> 00:27:48,199
- We are passing within
1,200 miles of you.

855
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:49,401
- This is Luna Three.

856
00:27:49,401 --> 00:27:52,637
We have established
visual contact with you.

857
00:27:52,637 --> 00:27:54,406
- That's the Sinus Roris crater.

858
00:27:54,406 --> 00:27:55,974
- Hope there's a
good place to park.

859
00:27:55,974 --> 00:27:58,510
- On the top of
it is Luna Three.

860
00:28:02,113 --> 00:28:04,416
- There's the solar reflector.

861
00:28:04,416 --> 00:28:06,484
They're signaling us.

862
00:28:06,484 --> 00:28:09,487
- [Servo] Oh, blue moon,
you saw me standing alone.

863
00:28:09,487 --> 00:28:11,156
- Without a dream in her heart.

864
00:28:12,557 --> 00:28:14,693
- [Joel] Without
a love of her own.

865
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:16,594
- That's where her husband fell.

866
00:28:17,495 --> 00:28:19,030
I brought him back to the camp

867
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,665
but he was already dead.

868
00:28:20,665 --> 00:28:22,400
- He was all busted up outside.

869
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,702
- We were friends.

870
00:28:23,702 --> 00:28:27,906
You know, Sumiko is
a wonderful woman.

871
00:28:27,906 --> 00:28:29,541
- This is Luna Three.

872
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:31,009
- [Servo] Quit clowning
around and get back to work.

873
00:28:31,009 --> 00:28:33,411
- I picked up unexpected swarms
of meteorites on our radar.

874
00:28:33,411 --> 00:28:36,748
Their present trajectory shows
that they may cross your path

875
00:28:36,748 --> 00:28:38,750
and be very dangerous.

876
00:28:38,750 --> 00:28:39,984
- We are receiving you.

877
00:28:39,984 --> 00:28:41,820
- But we can only
hear your chin.

878
00:28:41,820 --> 00:28:43,288
- Here are the
trajectory coordinates

879
00:28:43,288 --> 00:28:45,557
and orbital philosophy.

880
00:28:45,557 --> 00:28:48,860
Alpha X, seven
degrees, two minutes.

881
00:28:48,860 --> 00:28:51,563
Beta Epsilon, 48 degrees.

882
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:53,031
42 minutes.

883
00:28:53,031 --> 00:28:54,265
- [Servo] Now, here's
Geordie with the weather.

884
00:28:54,265 --> 00:28:56,401
- Listen, I've had an
extremely urgent message

885
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:57,335
from Luna Three.

886
00:28:57,335 --> 00:28:58,570
A meteorite warning.

887
00:28:58,570 --> 00:28:59,404
- Says you.

888
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:06,111
- Professor Sikarna, here's
the latest meteorite report.

889
00:29:06,111 --> 00:29:09,047
Alpha X, seven
degrees, two minutes.

890
00:29:09,047 --> 00:29:13,985
Beta Epsilon, 48
degrees, 42 minutes.

891
00:29:15,887 --> 00:29:18,490
- The meteorite swarm
should reach us in 48 hours,

892
00:29:18,490 --> 00:29:19,724
at the latest.

893
00:29:19,724 --> 00:29:22,494
- [Joel] Hey, wasn't
he on Mork and Mindy.

894
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:24,796
- Keep close radio
contact with Luna Three.

895
00:29:24,796 --> 00:29:27,265
- And the seventh caller
will get a free album.

896
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,500
- Calling Luna Three.

897
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:30,034
We've received your
meteorite warning.

898
00:29:30,034 --> 00:29:31,970
We'll be sending you regular
coordinates of our course...

899
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:34,105
(all mock shouting)

900
00:29:34,105 --> 00:29:37,008
(soft tense music)

901
00:29:38,209 --> 00:29:40,378
- This is the beginning
of my personal log book.

902
00:29:40,378 --> 00:29:42,614
- [Joel] Mr. Toothbrush,
you're the only one

903
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:44,415
who really understands me.

904
00:29:44,415 --> 00:29:45,583
- Of the Cosmostraiter.

905
00:29:45,583 --> 00:29:48,486
The computer is keeping
us on our course.

906
00:29:48,486 --> 00:29:51,322
In case of unforeseen
circumstances,

907
00:29:51,322 --> 00:29:53,291
it can take immediate decisions

908
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:56,327
to alter our speed or direction.

909
00:29:56,327 --> 00:29:58,696
This electronic brain
will be our pilot

910
00:29:58,696 --> 00:29:59,931
for the next 30 days.

911
00:29:59,931 --> 00:30:01,199
- [Servo] And our friend.

912
00:30:01,199 --> 00:30:02,133
- Because no human
being could handle

913
00:30:02,133 --> 00:30:03,668
the immensely complex machines

914
00:30:03,668 --> 00:30:05,470
of the spaceship by himself.

915
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,738
- Expect Steve Allen.

916
00:30:06,738 --> 00:30:08,773
- To now, we have
covered a distance

917
00:30:08,773 --> 00:30:11,476
of 2,600,000 miles.

918
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:12,744
- [Servo] Your mileage may vary.

919
00:30:12,744 --> 00:30:15,346
- Dr. Omigura is noting
our reactions carefully

920
00:30:15,346 --> 00:30:17,849
and keeping close check on
our health and well being.

921
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:19,551
A special liquid food,

922
00:30:19,551 --> 00:30:22,086
which can easily be absorbed
in a state of no gravity

923
00:30:22,086 --> 00:30:24,656
is proving very
successful with all of us.

924
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:25,857
- [Joel] And she's
got a lot of fun stuff

925
00:30:25,857 --> 00:30:27,025
to keep us busy, too.

926
00:30:28,426 --> 00:30:30,528
- French dressing, I love it.

927
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:33,865
- Our chief engineer
spends most of his time

928
00:30:33,865 --> 00:30:36,334
in his machine shop,
testing his automats

929
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:37,635
over and over again.

930
00:30:37,635 --> 00:30:38,803
- [Servo] Oh come on,
that's a rock tumbler.

931
00:30:38,803 --> 00:30:40,371
- It is thanks to them

932
00:30:40,371 --> 00:30:42,707
and to the fact that they
are in perfect running order

933
00:30:42,707 --> 00:30:45,443
that we are relieved
of many tiresome tasks.

934
00:30:45,443 --> 00:30:46,511
- Like acting.

935
00:30:47,912 --> 00:30:50,415
- Our expert in cybernetics
has to be everywhere.

936
00:30:50,415 --> 00:30:53,284
He is one of the key
men of the expedition.

937
00:30:53,284 --> 00:30:55,220
- [Joel] All right, all right.

938
00:30:55,220 --> 00:30:56,054
I'll get it.

939
00:30:56,054 --> 00:30:57,655
I'm coming.

940
00:30:57,655 --> 00:30:59,324
- Professor Sikarna
devotes all his time

941
00:30:59,324 --> 00:31:00,692
to the message from Venus.

942
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:02,093
He and T'chen Yu are trying

943
00:31:02,093 --> 00:31:03,561
to decipher the damaged spool

944
00:31:03,561 --> 00:31:06,130
which means they spend
long hours at the markets.

945
00:31:06,130 --> 00:31:07,398
- [Servo] In little
yellow boots.

946
00:31:07,398 --> 00:31:09,367
- The electronic brain
is working night and day

947
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:11,402
but no can be sure what
the result will be.

948
00:31:11,402 --> 00:31:13,438
(mock shouting)

949
00:31:13,438 --> 00:31:16,341
(soft tense music)

950
00:31:21,012 --> 00:31:22,247
- Harringway, our commander,

951
00:31:22,247 --> 00:31:23,848
is keeping a constant
check on our course.

952
00:31:23,848 --> 00:31:26,084
- Well, this is the last
of the bathroom tissue.;

953
00:31:26,084 --> 00:31:27,585
- Was active last night.

954
00:31:27,585 --> 00:31:30,889
It switched the rockets
on for nearly 17 seconds.

955
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,690
- [Servo] Oh, I'm impressed.

956
00:31:32,690 --> 00:31:34,492
- Perhaps to avoid
the meteor swarm.

957
00:31:34,492 --> 00:31:37,195
- We won't be running
into it till tomorrow.

958
00:31:38,630 --> 00:31:41,299
- Looks like your automats
don't have the same idea

959
00:31:41,299 --> 00:31:42,267
that you do.

960
00:31:42,267 --> 00:31:43,268
- [Servo] They make sandwiches.

961
00:31:44,702 --> 00:31:46,237
- [Joel] Dear, toothbrush.

962
00:31:46,237 --> 00:31:48,506
- Professor Orloff is an
enthusiastic chess player.

963
00:31:48,506 --> 00:31:49,474
- [Servo] Doh.

964
00:31:49,474 --> 00:31:50,775
- He has beaten all of us

965
00:31:50,775 --> 00:31:53,578
but I think he's found
his master in Omigow.

966
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:54,712
- [Servo] King me.

967
00:31:56,347 --> 00:31:57,649
- King G 8.

968
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:00,985
- [Servo] Line.

969
00:32:00,985 --> 00:32:02,520
Line, please.

970
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:03,588
Line!

971
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,089
- [Robot] King E6.

972
00:32:08,426 --> 00:32:09,661
(Crow laughing robotically)

973
00:32:09,661 --> 00:32:11,396
- Take that, pink boy.

974
00:32:11,396 --> 00:32:12,830
- It's amazing.

975
00:32:12,830 --> 00:32:14,832
He plays his end
game wonderfully.

976
00:32:14,832 --> 00:32:16,334
- [Joel] Boy, do I stink.

977
00:32:16,334 --> 00:32:17,869
- I thought that I had got him

978
00:32:17,869 --> 00:32:19,103
but you see, he's
put his king on E6

979
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:21,506
and I'm forced into
the corner at H8.

980
00:32:21,506 --> 00:32:24,409
(whimsical music)

981
00:32:24,409 --> 00:32:25,777
- Good evening and welcome

982
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:28,846
to Alfred Hitchcock presents.

983
00:32:28,846 --> 00:32:30,515
Just uh, just that joke.

984
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:31,416
- [Joel] Good one.

985
00:32:31,416 --> 00:32:32,917
- [Robot] King E7.

986
00:32:34,085 --> 00:32:35,820
Checkmate, next move.

987
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:39,057
- [Servo] Oh, I'll
alert the media.

988
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,428
- [Joel] He's a kookster.

989
00:32:43,428 --> 00:32:47,332
(goofy whimsical music)

990
00:32:47,332 --> 00:32:49,968
- That is the 10th
match that I've lost.

991
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:51,202
I should give up, I guess.

992
00:32:51,202 --> 00:32:52,704
- That's the spirit.

993
00:32:52,704 --> 00:32:54,572
- I would suggest that you
make an improvement in Omigow.

994
00:32:54,572 --> 00:32:55,840
- Oh really?

995
00:32:55,840 --> 00:32:58,242
- If he only had a heart.

996
00:32:58,242 --> 00:32:59,811
- A brain.
- A home.

997
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:02,513
- [Servo] Da nerve.

998
00:33:02,513 --> 00:33:05,984
- Don't you think you
could be able to do that?

999
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,486
Just a little bit
of heart, Jerome.

1000
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:10,955
- [Servo] Yes, I
think I could do that.

1001
00:33:12,590 --> 00:33:14,892
- Oh, he'll do anything to win.

1002
00:33:16,394 --> 00:33:17,328
- [Servo] The dryers off kilter.

1003
00:33:17,328 --> 00:33:19,063
- [Joel] Whoa, bonny's done.

1004
00:33:19,063 --> 00:33:20,231
- [Servo] Fries are up.

1005
00:33:21,232 --> 00:33:24,335
- [Joel] Irwin Allen presents.

1006
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:25,903
- Chock full of nuts.

1007
00:33:25,903 --> 00:33:28,406
- [Servo] Guess somebody forgot
to set the parking break.

1008
00:33:28,406 --> 00:33:31,109
(tense music)

1009
00:33:31,109 --> 00:33:32,343
- Big one.

1010
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:33,745
- Quick, switch on
the emergency gyro.

1011
00:33:35,146 --> 00:33:36,514
- [Joel] Pop-o-matic
pops the dice,

1012
00:33:36,514 --> 00:33:37,949
pop the six and you move twice.

1013
00:33:37,949 --> 00:33:39,150
Race your men around the track

1014
00:33:39,150 --> 00:33:40,184
and try to send the others back.

1015
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:42,320
That's pop-o-matic trouble.

1016
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:44,822
(tense music)

1017
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:48,693
- [Servo] Somebody get that?

1018
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:49,527
- I'm here, Steve.

1019
00:33:51,329 --> 00:33:52,430
- [Servo] Oh.

1020
00:33:52,430 --> 00:33:53,631
- [Joel] Hold me, Steve, again.

1021
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:54,599
- Is that your leg?

1022
00:33:57,135 --> 00:33:59,704
- [Servo] Well, fries are done.

1023
00:34:06,244 --> 00:34:07,879
Get off of me.

1024
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:10,915
- Brinkmann, see if T'Chen
Yu and Sikarna are all right.

1025
00:34:10,915 --> 00:34:12,083
- [Joel] What about us?

1026
00:34:15,586 --> 00:34:16,454
- [Servo] Oh.

1027
00:34:16,454 --> 00:34:19,457
(tense music)

1028
00:34:19,457 --> 00:34:21,025
- How could this happen?

1029
00:34:21,025 --> 00:34:22,260
- [Joel] There.

1030
00:34:22,260 --> 00:34:23,494
- I thought that
the Cosmostraiter

1031
00:34:23,494 --> 00:34:24,962
was able to avoid meteor
storms automatically.

1032
00:34:24,962 --> 00:34:26,564
- [Joel] Now you can play
flag football anytime.

1033
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:27,799
- She didn't react
quickly enough.

1034
00:34:27,799 --> 00:34:30,001
She was regulated to a
shower under mass eight.

1035
00:34:30,001 --> 00:34:31,836
That was why we had to
switch on the emergency...

1036
00:34:31,836 --> 00:34:33,037
- [Servo] Yeah, yeah, whatever.

1037
00:34:33,037 --> 00:34:35,540
(tense music)

1038
00:34:38,342 --> 00:34:40,812
- Orloff, how much
course deviation?

1039
00:34:40,812 --> 00:34:42,713
- [Servo] What, personally?

1040
00:34:44,115 --> 00:34:45,950
So the four, carry the seven.

1041
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:48,086
Boy, we're in debt
up to our eyeballs.

1042
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:52,056
- 12 degrees, 17 minutes.

1043
00:34:52,056 --> 00:34:53,591
- Our speed?

1044
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:54,525
- Constant.

1045
00:34:54,525 --> 00:34:55,827
Eight point two miles a second.

1046
00:34:55,827 --> 00:34:57,328
- My hair?

1047
00:34:57,328 --> 00:34:58,830
Fully coiffed, sir.

1048
00:34:58,830 --> 00:35:00,465
- I guess the main principle
swarm will be on us soon.

1049
00:35:00,465 --> 00:35:03,901
If we continue at maximum
speed, it will mean disaster.

1050
00:35:03,901 --> 00:35:05,103
(goofy tense music)

1051
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:06,904
- [Joel] And stopped
that nutty horn section.

1052
00:35:06,904 --> 00:35:08,139
- Decelerate.

1053
00:35:08,139 --> 00:35:10,741
(upbeat music)

1054
00:35:14,445 --> 00:35:16,080
(tense music)

1055
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,815
- Well, I can't think
of a better bunch

1056
00:35:17,815 --> 00:35:19,083
of people to die with.

1057
00:35:19,083 --> 00:35:20,251
- What do you mean the
motors aren't working?

1058
00:35:20,251 --> 00:35:21,953
What's the matter, Durand?

1059
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:23,955
- [Joel] They're
not working, sir.

1060
00:35:26,657 --> 00:35:27,925
- [Servo] Come on.

1061
00:35:27,925 --> 00:35:29,460
Just put a penny in
the fusebox, baldy.

1062
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:30,895
Come on.

1063
00:35:30,895 --> 00:35:32,497
- A meteor fragment has
damaged the deceleration unit.

1064
00:35:32,497 --> 00:35:33,898
We have to go outside

1065
00:35:33,898 --> 00:35:34,899
and try and repair
it right away.

1066
00:35:34,899 --> 00:35:37,435
- Outside, in this weather?

1067
00:35:37,435 --> 00:35:39,504
- How long before the
main swarm hits us?

1068
00:35:39,504 --> 00:35:40,438
- I can't say.

1069
00:35:40,438 --> 00:35:41,672
It may be on us any second now.

1070
00:35:41,672 --> 00:35:43,407
- Brinkmann, will you help me?

1071
00:35:43,407 --> 00:35:46,844
- Professor Sikarna and
T'chen Yu, are you all right.

1072
00:35:46,844 --> 00:35:48,079
- No bones broken.

1073
00:35:48,079 --> 00:35:49,881
- [Joel] You know,
I hurt my head.

1074
00:35:49,881 --> 00:35:51,382
- Please give me our
present deviation,

1075
00:35:51,382 --> 00:35:53,684
direction coordinates,
and corrected course.

1076
00:35:53,684 --> 00:35:54,886
- [Servo] In that order.

1077
00:35:56,287 --> 00:35:58,589
- Hey, a human and a salt
shaker fused into one.

1078
00:35:58,589 --> 00:36:00,358
That will put some
spice in his life.

1079
00:36:00,358 --> 00:36:01,492
(laughing)

1080
00:36:01,492 --> 00:36:02,660
- [Joel] Good one.

1081
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:03,494
- Sorry.

1082
00:36:07,732 --> 00:36:09,934
- [Servo] Um, hey, I
gotta go to the bathroom.

1083
00:36:09,934 --> 00:36:11,502
- Just go in the suit.

1084
00:36:11,502 --> 00:36:12,737
- [Servo] Oh.

1085
00:36:12,737 --> 00:36:14,972
- And now it's time for
the $64,000 question.

1086
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:21,012
- [Servo] Bye.

1087
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:22,680
(alarm whooping)

1088
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:27,318
- [Joel] What a time to
get the whooping cough.

1089
00:36:27,318 --> 00:36:28,152
- Whoa.

1090
00:36:29,587 --> 00:36:31,822
Hey, he's transparent now.

1091
00:36:31,822 --> 00:36:34,792
(Tom laughing)

1092
00:36:34,792 --> 00:36:36,260
Oh.

1093
00:36:36,260 --> 00:36:40,398
- [Joel] You know, Bob doesn't
matte very well, does he?

1094
00:36:40,398 --> 00:36:42,900
(tense music)

1095
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:49,307
- Watch out.

1096
00:36:49,307 --> 00:36:50,808
Everybody fasten your belts.

1097
00:36:50,808 --> 00:36:53,511
- [Servo] Yeah, why don't you
stop breathing down my neck.

1098
00:36:55,413 --> 00:36:57,048
- No, uh uh.

1099
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:59,116
- Uh uh.
- No, no, no, no.

1100
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,154
- Stand by.

1101
00:37:03,154 --> 00:37:05,590
- Hey, look at him
squirm out there.

1102
00:37:05,590 --> 00:37:06,624
That's our Bob.

1103
00:37:06,624 --> 00:37:10,027
(tense music)
(alarm whooping)

1104
00:37:10,027 --> 00:37:11,229
- Is it safe to
start the motors yet?

1105
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,264
- [Servo] Can somebody
shoot that turkey?

1106
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:16,067
- Repair is completed.

1107
00:37:16,067 --> 00:37:17,101
Clear on back.

1108
00:37:17,101 --> 00:37:20,771
(all blubbering their lips)

1109
00:37:22,306 --> 00:37:24,308
- [Servo] Oh, all right.

1110
00:37:26,611 --> 00:37:28,512
- Cosmostraiter
calling Luna Three.

1111
00:37:28,512 --> 00:37:30,214
Cosmostraiter
calling Luna Three.

1112
00:37:30,214 --> 00:37:32,116
Meteor swarm has passed.

1113
00:37:32,116 --> 00:37:33,818
- That ought to hold 'em.

1114
00:37:33,818 --> 00:37:35,453
- Everything okay on board.

1115
00:37:35,453 --> 00:37:37,955
(tense music)

1116
00:37:41,025 --> 00:37:42,793
- [Joel] Space the final...

1117
00:37:42,793 --> 00:37:43,628
Huh?

1118
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:48,432
- [Narrator] Three
weeks have gone by

1119
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:49,800
since we left the Earth.

1120
00:37:49,800 --> 00:37:51,969
We should reach Venus
in about 10 days.

1121
00:37:51,969 --> 00:37:54,372
In spite of our enormous speed,

1122
00:37:54,372 --> 00:37:56,374
the stars seem to
hang motionless.

1123
00:37:56,374 --> 00:37:57,842
- [Servo] On black
construction paper.

1124
00:37:57,842 --> 00:37:59,076
- [Narrator] Disturbances
caused by the planet.

1125
00:37:59,076 --> 00:38:01,279
Radio contact with Earth
is no longer possible.

1126
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,680
- Hey, my boo boo is all better.

1127
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:04,282
- Too much interference.

1128
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:05,383
I can't hear a thing.

1129
00:38:05,383 --> 00:38:06,384
- Keep trying.

1130
00:38:08,085 --> 00:38:09,520
- [Joel] He's right, you know.

1131
00:38:10,821 --> 00:38:13,257
- Alpha X, 32
degrees, eight minute.

1132
00:38:13,257 --> 00:38:16,794
B to Y, seven degrees.

1133
00:38:16,794 --> 00:38:18,329
- You sunk my battleship.

1134
00:38:18,329 --> 00:38:20,631
- [Joel] You know, they're
backstage all of a sudden.

1135
00:38:20,631 --> 00:38:22,700
- What are you doing?

1136
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:24,101
- It's a booger.

1137
00:38:24,101 --> 00:38:25,903
- I'm making a heart for Omigow.

1138
00:38:25,903 --> 00:38:29,907
10 consecutive defeats are
driving our friend crazy.

1139
00:38:29,907 --> 00:38:31,475
I want him to enjoy
his favorite game.

1140
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:32,710
- [Joel] Hmm, thoughtful.

1141
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:35,146
- I would you to do
something, also, for me.

1142
00:38:35,146 --> 00:38:37,548
It would be nice to see
you eat occasionally.

1143
00:38:37,548 --> 00:38:39,717
- [Joel] It's western
french, I made it myself.

1144
00:38:40,818 --> 00:38:42,820
- Sikarna said exactly
the same thing.

1145
00:38:51,495 --> 00:38:52,430
Professor.

1146
00:38:52,430 --> 00:38:53,230
- Well, I poisoned the doctor.

1147
00:38:53,230 --> 00:38:54,999
- What do you want?

1148
00:38:54,999 --> 00:38:56,100
Please, not now.

1149
00:38:56,100 --> 00:38:57,268
- [Joel] Well.

1150
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:00,638
- Your health is
my responsibility

1151
00:39:00,638 --> 00:39:01,839
and you haven't eaten for days.

1152
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:03,908
- I haven't a second to spare.

1153
00:39:03,908 --> 00:39:06,811
- [Joel] Not even for
creamy dill and chive?

1154
00:39:06,811 --> 00:39:08,913
- [Servo] How do you like
my new mood synthesizers?

1155
00:39:08,913 --> 00:39:11,215
(ethereal electronic tones)

1156
00:39:11,215 --> 00:39:14,185
- [Joel] Wow, Steve always
drinks my dressing my home.

1157
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:15,086
Well, it's time to cut my hair

1158
00:39:15,086 --> 00:39:16,320
and get into a pantsuit.

1159
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:18,022
- Sumiko.

1160
00:39:20,624 --> 00:39:22,526
You mustn't insist,
he's nervous.

1161
00:39:22,526 --> 00:39:24,795
He's having a very hard
time with that spool.

1162
00:39:24,795 --> 00:39:25,863
You understand?

1163
00:39:25,863 --> 00:39:26,697
- [Joel] Oh, that's great.

1164
00:39:26,697 --> 00:39:27,698
Who are you, anyway?

1165
00:39:33,971 --> 00:39:36,640
- Knight, E6, check.

1166
00:39:36,640 --> 00:39:38,042
- Does this guy have a job?

1167
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,777
- [Servo] I don't think so.

1168
00:39:39,777 --> 00:39:43,948
(goofy whimsical music)

1169
00:39:43,948 --> 00:39:45,683
- He doesn't like that.

1170
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:46,951
- [Joel] It hurts him.

1171
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:49,553
- [Robot] King E8.

1172
00:39:49,553 --> 00:39:51,555
- [Servo] Think the ink?

1173
00:39:52,857 --> 00:39:53,691
- Mate.

1174
00:39:55,259 --> 00:39:56,260
- Congratulations.

1175
00:39:56,260 --> 00:39:58,129
You've won at last.

1176
00:39:58,129 --> 00:40:00,264
(all mock goofy laughing)

1177
00:40:00,264 --> 00:40:01,766
- [Joel] Oh, fun.

1178
00:40:01,766 --> 00:40:03,300
- Classical end play, I
think you deserve to win.

1179
00:40:04,168 --> 00:40:05,002
- Oh, quit kissing up.

1180
00:40:05,002 --> 00:40:06,003
- He plays a good game.

1181
00:40:06,003 --> 00:40:07,338
He's not very easy to beat.

1182
00:40:08,539 --> 00:40:10,007
- But I did it at last.

1183
00:40:10,007 --> 00:40:11,542
Man has defeated the machine.

1184
00:40:11,542 --> 00:40:13,544
- Ah, too much heart.

1185
00:40:13,544 --> 00:40:15,179
- [Servo] That's right,
maybe I care too much.

1186
00:40:15,179 --> 00:40:16,013
- Want to try?

1187
00:40:16,013 --> 00:40:17,481
- Well, why not?

1188
00:40:17,481 --> 00:40:19,016
- [Intercom] Will you all
come to the marrocks, please?

1189
00:40:19,016 --> 00:40:21,018
- [Servo] That's how it starts.

1190
00:40:21,018 --> 00:40:22,820
- It's a cosmic document.

1191
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:24,188
- [Joel] All right.

1192
00:40:24,188 --> 00:40:25,790
- Hope there's no postage due.

1193
00:40:25,790 --> 00:40:29,360
- [Joel] Lite-Brite,
making things with light.

1194
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:30,461
Out of sight.

1195
00:40:30,461 --> 00:40:33,297
Making things with Lite-Brite.

1196
00:40:33,297 --> 00:40:34,899
- Hey, it's a John Tesh song.

1197
00:40:34,899 --> 00:40:37,535
- They have finally deciphered
the last part of the spool.

1198
00:40:37,535 --> 00:40:39,937
It gives complete meaning
to the cosmic document.

1199
00:40:41,372 --> 00:40:44,775
- [Servo] It says
(goofy warbling).

1200
00:40:44,775 --> 00:40:49,246
(indistinct warbled
electronic voice)

1201
00:40:57,388 --> 00:41:00,391
- [Joel] Well, it
uh, it gets better.

1202
00:41:02,026 --> 00:41:04,128
Well, that's neat but we got
to get back to the lunch room.

1203
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:05,696
- I will translate.

1204
00:41:05,696 --> 00:41:07,932
(all mock goofy warbling)

1205
00:41:07,932 --> 00:41:09,333
We will initially
subject the planet

1206
00:41:09,333 --> 00:41:12,870
to a very intense
bombardment of radiation.

1207
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:15,072
Conquest and
occupation of the Earth

1208
00:41:15,072 --> 00:41:17,208
will then present no difficulty.

1209
00:41:17,208 --> 00:41:18,809
When the ionization...

1210
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,177
- Oh, he's reading Dianetics.

1211
00:41:20,177 --> 00:41:23,013
- The final extermination
phase can start.

1212
00:41:23,013 --> 00:41:24,949
- This can only mean...

1213
00:41:26,083 --> 00:41:27,218
An Attack!

1214
00:41:27,218 --> 00:41:28,219
(tense music)

1215
00:41:28,219 --> 00:41:29,153
Against our planet.

1216
00:41:29,153 --> 00:41:30,387
- [Servo] With tympanies.

1217
00:41:30,387 --> 00:41:31,889
- An invasion by the
inhabitants of Venus.

1218
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:34,825
- The cosmic document was
not intended for us to read.

1219
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:37,595
It's a cold blooded
blueprint of destruction.

1220
00:41:37,595 --> 00:41:38,863
- Maybe we could--
- We must inform the Earth.

1221
00:41:38,863 --> 00:41:40,931
I'll try and make contact.

1222
00:41:40,931 --> 00:41:41,765
- But I--

1223
00:41:41,765 --> 00:41:42,633
- Wait, Cal.

1224
00:41:42,633 --> 00:41:44,201
- No, let him try.

1225
00:41:44,201 --> 00:41:45,970
- Will it do the Earth any
good to know what we know?

1226
00:41:45,970 --> 00:41:48,239
- The Earth is in danger,
we must warn them.

1227
00:41:48,239 --> 00:41:49,907
- [Joel] Well at least
we should try and go--

1228
00:41:49,907 --> 00:41:52,243
- No, our planet
was in peril before

1229
00:41:52,243 --> 00:41:54,478
they discovered the spool
and nothing happened.

1230
00:41:54,478 --> 00:41:55,312
- [Servo] He's right, it's--

1231
00:41:55,312 --> 00:41:56,814
- That's an argument.

1232
00:41:56,814 --> 00:41:59,383
As we haven't any idea how
the Venusian's calculate time.

1233
00:41:59,383 --> 00:42:00,818
- [Joel] Well at least we can--

1234
00:42:00,818 --> 00:42:02,286
- If the Earth knew of the
terrible danger threatening her,

1235
00:42:02,286 --> 00:42:06,156
unrest and even hysteria
would spread like wild fire

1236
00:42:06,156 --> 00:42:09,527
from pole to pole, the whole
world would be in a panic.

1237
00:42:10,394 --> 00:42:12,329
- [Joel] That's two poles.

1238
00:42:12,329 --> 00:42:13,797
- No, no Orloff.

1239
00:42:13,797 --> 00:42:15,766
I'm convinced you're wrong.

1240
00:42:15,766 --> 00:42:17,868
- [Joel] Oh just shut
him out like that, sure.

1241
00:42:17,868 --> 00:42:19,570
- For years and years, the
whole of the human race

1242
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:21,138
faced the danger of atomic war.

1243
00:42:21,138 --> 00:42:21,939
- Yes.

1244
00:42:21,939 --> 00:42:23,207
- And they survived.

1245
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:25,743
Not through ignorance
but through knowledge.

1246
00:42:25,743 --> 00:42:27,845
Because they knew
what the danger was.

1247
00:42:30,948 --> 00:42:31,782
No.

1248
00:42:31,782 --> 00:42:33,551
There won't be a panic.

1249
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:35,886
(all mock screaming)

1250
00:42:35,886 --> 00:42:37,254
T'chen Yu, don't
you agree with me?

1251
00:42:38,689 --> 00:42:42,026
- I am sure that if we meet
the inhabitants of Venus,

1252
00:42:42,026 --> 00:42:44,562
we'll be able to convince
that it would be folly

1253
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:45,729
to start that war.

1254
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:46,864
- [Servo] Yeah, right.

1255
00:42:46,864 --> 00:42:48,332
- So, try to contact the Earth.

1256
00:42:48,332 --> 00:42:50,834
- [Joel] They're not
home, I left a message.

1257
00:42:50,834 --> 00:42:51,802
- I can't get through.

1258
00:42:51,802 --> 00:42:52,903
Too much disturbance from Venus.

1259
00:42:52,903 --> 00:42:55,205
Our signals are distorted.

1260
00:42:55,205 --> 00:42:57,274
(tense music)

1261
00:42:57,274 --> 00:42:59,910
The Earth won't hear us.

1262
00:42:59,910 --> 00:43:02,680
- I said, the Earth
won't hear us.

1263
00:43:03,914 --> 00:43:05,115
- [Joel] I'm filled with shame.

1264
00:43:05,115 --> 00:43:06,250
- Well, what do you say?

1265
00:43:06,250 --> 00:43:08,385
Should we turn back to Earth?

1266
00:43:08,385 --> 00:43:10,421
- [Servo] Oh and end
this dream vacation?

1267
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:12,590
- No.

1268
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:18,729
(all shouting)

1269
00:43:20,297 --> 00:43:21,498
- Return?

1270
00:43:21,498 --> 00:43:23,434
- [Servo] Oh, I don't think so.

1271
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,436
- Never.

1272
00:43:27,471 --> 00:43:28,405
- [Servo] Cowardly retreat?

1273
00:43:28,405 --> 00:43:30,474
Oh please sign me up for that.

1274
00:43:32,376 --> 00:43:33,210
- Uh uh.

1275
00:43:36,113 --> 00:43:38,549
- [Joel] All right then,
we've got a war to fight.

1276
00:43:38,549 --> 00:43:39,750
- Durand, our speed.

1277
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:42,920
- 31,000 miles per hour.

1278
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:44,688
In three days, we reach Venus.

1279
00:43:44,688 --> 00:43:46,757
- Good, Teller check our course.

1280
00:43:46,757 --> 00:43:48,025
- [Joel] Yes, it's
good, isn't it?

1281
00:43:48,025 --> 00:43:49,660
- Orloff.
- Yes, that will be good.

1282
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:50,828
- [Servo] Let's roll, guys.

1283
00:43:50,828 --> 00:43:52,029
- [Joel] Oh, we better
get out of here.

1284
00:43:52,029 --> 00:43:53,597
- Radiation is
reaching steadily.

1285
00:43:53,597 --> 00:43:54,798
I'll recheck.

1286
00:43:54,798 --> 00:43:55,566
- Mr. Crusher, take
us out of warp.

1287
00:44:00,371 --> 00:44:02,940
