1352
00:45:46,110 --> 00:45:47,244
Yeah, you idiot.

1353
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:48,712
That's right.

1354
00:45:48,712 --> 00:45:50,514
Still dumber than a bag
full of hammers, aren't you?

1355
00:45:50,514 --> 00:45:51,381
Yeah.

1356
00:45:51,381 --> 00:45:52,583
Now, listen Tom.

1357
00:45:52,583 --> 00:45:53,751
- Okay.

1358
00:45:53,751 --> 00:45:55,152
- I know you're scared
out of your wits

1359
00:45:55,152 --> 00:45:58,122
but I need you to sign
that gorilla a song.

1360
00:45:58,122 --> 00:46:01,091
What's that song you sang
last Wednesday at Vespers?

1361
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:02,292
- Oh sweet mother of mine.

1362
00:46:02,292 --> 00:46:03,093
But I don't understand
how that's gonna--

1363
00:46:03,093 --> 00:46:04,328
- Yeah, no buts, Tom.

1364
00:46:04,328 --> 00:46:05,763
Just start singing, boy.

1365
00:46:05,763 --> 00:46:06,597
- Okay.

1366
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,165
Oh, nice gorilla.

1367
00:46:08,165 --> 00:46:12,469
Oh nice boy, you crummy
monkey with matted awful--

1368
00:46:12,469 --> 00:46:14,271
- Hey, Tom, watch it.

1369
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:17,207
♪ Oh sweet mother of mine 

1370
00:46:17,207 --> 00:46:21,845
♪ Tis only for you I pine 

1371
00:46:21,845 --> 00:46:23,914
♪ I'll try to get bail 

1372
00:46:23,914 --> 00:46:25,883
♪ And I'll drive up to jail 

1373
00:46:25,883 --> 00:46:27,251
♪ And I'll spring 

1374
00:46:27,251 --> 00:46:30,921
♪ That sweet mother of mine 

1375
00:46:32,256 --> 00:46:33,857
- You sang that at Vespers?

1376
00:46:33,857 --> 00:46:35,592
- What in the world
is going on here?

1377
00:46:35,592 --> 00:46:37,294
- Oh Joel, there was a
gorilla at the screen.

1378
00:46:37,294 --> 00:46:39,696
He was looking at us
and he made us sad.

1379
00:46:39,696 --> 00:46:42,132
- Just take it, take it easy.

1380
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:45,068
Take it easy, you guys.

1381
00:46:45,068 --> 00:46:47,371
Take a breath, come
on, take a breath.

1382
00:46:47,371 --> 00:46:48,806
We got movie sign!

1383
00:46:48,806 --> 00:46:51,975
(crying and shouting)

1384
00:46:59,750 --> 00:47:00,684
- [Servo] He was big and sweaty.

1385
00:47:00,684 --> 00:47:01,485
- [Joel] A gorilla in space?

1386
00:47:01,485 --> 00:47:02,419
I don't know.

1387
00:47:02,419 --> 00:47:03,220
- [Servo] It was really there.

1388
00:47:03,220 --> 00:47:04,154
- We really saw one.

1389
00:47:04,154 --> 00:47:05,689
It looked like Gino Vannelli.

1390
00:47:05,689 --> 00:47:07,124
- [Servo] It was terrible.

1391
00:47:07,124 --> 00:47:07,524
- All our efforts to
communicate with the Earth

1392
00:47:08,692 --> 00:47:09,927
via Luna Three have
been unsuccessful.

1393
00:47:09,927 --> 00:47:11,461
- [Joel] I love you,
goofy toothbrush.

1394
00:47:11,461 --> 00:47:13,130
- We started to accelerate
by means of rocket motors.

1395
00:47:13,130 --> 00:47:15,032
Professor Harringway
is guiding the ship

1396
00:47:15,032 --> 00:47:17,000
into an elliptical
orbit around Venus.

1397
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,970
We are now a satellite
of this silent planet.

1398
00:47:19,970 --> 00:47:21,538
- [Servo] Tell me
something we don't know.

1399
00:47:21,538 --> 00:47:23,006
- Are still trying, but in vain,

1400
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:24,942
to establish radio contact
with her inhabitants.

1401
00:47:24,942 --> 00:47:27,978
A thick wall of clouds
surrounds the planet.

1402
00:47:29,947 --> 00:47:31,014
- [Servo] Good morning.

1403
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,583
- 3,500 miles.

1404
00:47:32,583 --> 00:47:33,917
- [Joel] Thank you, Sulu.

1405
00:47:33,917 --> 00:47:36,353
- First analysis,
Venus atmosphere.

1406
00:47:36,353 --> 00:47:41,325
27% carbon dioxide,
14% formaldehyde.

1407
00:47:41,325 --> 00:47:43,126
- The air, the
air is everywhere.

1408
00:47:43,126 --> 00:47:44,394
- No oxygen,
atmosphere poisonous.

1409
00:47:44,394 --> 00:47:47,431
- We're faced with a
difficult decision.

1410
00:47:47,431 --> 00:47:50,934
As you know, we can only
land and take off once.

1411
00:47:50,934 --> 00:47:53,570
No point in taking any
unnecessary chances.

1412
00:47:53,570 --> 00:47:56,340
So one of us has got
to go ahead as scout.

1413
00:47:56,340 --> 00:47:57,274
- 2,000 miles.

1414
00:47:57,274 --> 00:47:58,208
- We're close enough now.

1415
00:47:58,208 --> 00:47:59,276
I'll go in the crawl-o-copter.

1416
00:47:59,276 --> 00:48:00,510
- Oh, the crawl-o-copter.

1417
00:48:00,510 --> 00:48:02,012
That's your answer
for everything.

1418
00:48:02,012 --> 00:48:04,147
- You have got to try and
find a landing place for us.

1419
00:48:04,147 --> 00:48:07,684
We'll stay in orbit at 150
miles altitude, all right?

1420
00:48:07,684 --> 00:48:09,152
- The crawl-o-copter's ready.

1421
00:48:09,152 --> 00:48:11,588
- [Servo] Oh everything's
better in the crawl-o-copter.

1422
00:48:11,588 --> 00:48:14,024
