contact with Brinkmann.

1529
00:52:14,131 --> 00:52:15,232
- And you should
all call each other

1530
00:52:15,232 --> 00:52:17,200
before the next costume party.

1531
00:52:17,200 --> 00:52:18,602
- Brinkmann calling
Cosmostraiter.

1532
00:52:18,602 --> 00:52:19,870
Please answer me, over.

1533
00:52:19,870 --> 00:52:21,905
- [Joel] This isn't
funny anymore, sirs.

1534
00:52:21,905 --> 00:52:24,774
(alarm blaring)

1535
00:52:24,774 --> 00:52:25,709
- Omigow.

1536
00:52:25,709 --> 00:52:26,743
- I'm bolting.

1537
00:52:26,743 --> 00:52:27,944
This is bogus.

1538
00:52:27,944 --> 00:52:29,613
- [Robot] Listening.

1539
00:52:31,014 --> 00:52:31,948
Be careful.

1540
00:52:33,049 --> 00:52:34,317
Danger.

1541
00:52:34,317 --> 00:52:36,086
- [Servo] Oh poison
gas for atmosphere?

1542
00:52:36,086 --> 00:52:37,821
Give me more of that.

1543
00:52:37,821 --> 00:52:39,623
- [Robot] Intense radiation.

1544
00:52:39,623 --> 00:52:42,893
Eight (mumbles).

1545
00:52:42,893 --> 00:52:44,528
- How long can we stay here?

1546
00:52:44,528 --> 00:52:46,596
- About three minutes ago.

1547
00:52:46,596 --> 00:52:49,366
- [Robot] Eight minutes maximum.

1548
00:52:49,366 --> 00:52:51,034
- Turn back, Omigow.

1549
00:52:52,035 --> 00:52:53,136
- [Joel] bidi, bidi.

1550
00:52:53,136 --> 00:52:55,672
Thanks for the promotion, jerk.

1551
00:52:57,507 --> 00:53:00,243
- Cosmostraiter, Cosmostraiter.

1552
00:53:00,243 --> 00:53:01,912
I don't hear you.

1553
00:53:01,912 --> 00:53:03,446
- Come on guys, stop it.

1554
00:53:03,446 --> 00:53:04,414
Stop mocking me.

1555
00:53:04,414 --> 00:53:05,815
- Hello, hello?

1556
00:53:05,815 --> 00:53:07,217
Do you hear me?

1557
00:53:08,518 --> 00:53:10,086
This blasted radioactive forest

1558
00:53:10,086 --> 00:53:11,688
won't let radio waves through.

1559
00:53:13,657 --> 00:53:15,425
Go on, Omigow, go on.

1560
00:53:16,626 --> 00:53:19,262
- [Joel] bidi bidi
bidi, beat cheeks.

1561
00:53:20,230 --> 00:53:22,465
- Keep on.
- Keep going, that's it.

1562
00:53:22,465 --> 00:53:23,800
Keep going.

1563
00:53:23,800 --> 00:53:26,903
(explosion)
(all shouting)

1564
00:53:26,903 --> 00:53:29,806
(dramatic music)

1565
00:53:29,806 --> 00:53:30,840
- Hold it, Omigow.

1566
00:53:30,840 --> 00:53:32,108
They're attacking us.

1567
00:53:32,108 --> 00:53:34,411
- It turns out he was
flying a Pinto-copter.

1568
00:53:35,278 --> 00:53:36,313
- Do you hear me?

1569
00:53:36,313 --> 00:53:38,548
The crawl-o-copter's exploded.

1570
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:39,382
- A flash.

1571
00:53:40,817 --> 00:53:43,053
- [Servo] Oh I think that was
probably Bob cashing it in.

1572
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:44,054
- What was it?

1573
00:53:45,188 --> 00:53:46,122
- I don't know.

1574
00:53:46,122 --> 00:53:47,657
Computer shows a pressure wave.

1575
00:53:47,657 --> 00:53:49,226
Apparently an explosion.

1576
00:53:49,226 --> 00:53:51,328
Distance, 120 miles.

1577
00:53:53,730 --> 00:53:55,198
- Brinkmann.

1578
00:53:55,198 --> 00:53:57,734
- Or it could be a signal
from the Venusians.

1579
00:53:57,734 --> 00:53:59,002
- [Joel] Or Bob's fiery death.

1580
00:53:59,002 --> 00:54:00,637
- We better land at
once, as best we can.

1581
00:54:01,838 --> 00:54:04,507
Talua, make a careful
check on our position

1582
00:54:04,507 --> 00:54:06,409
and try to contact Brinkmann.

1583
00:54:06,409 --> 00:54:07,677
- [Servo] Yeah, yeah.

1584
00:54:07,677 --> 00:54:08,912
When I get to it,
when I get to it.

1585
00:54:08,912 --> 00:54:11,948
(tense music)

1586
00:54:11,948 --> 00:54:13,817
- Omigow, back here, quickly.

1587
00:54:16,987 --> 00:54:19,122
- Hey, the carpet broke.

1588
00:54:19,122 --> 00:54:20,991
- [Joel] Oh boy, he's fallen

1589
00:54:22,259 --> 00:54:24,327
into a super ball test chamber.

1590
00:54:25,996 --> 00:54:27,731
Shopper always
leaves you laughing

1591
00:54:27,731 --> 00:54:29,132
ah-ha-ha-ha.

1592
00:54:31,001 --> 00:54:33,370
Yeah, it looks like
we got visitors, boys.

1593
00:54:36,673 --> 00:54:38,908
Come on, smart
boy, try your hand.

1594
00:54:38,908 --> 00:54:39,743
Come on.

1595
00:54:42,345 --> 00:54:44,281
Go ahead, I sit on the
right hand of the devil,

1596
00:54:44,281 --> 00:54:45,348
I am evil incarnate.

1597
00:54:45,348 --> 00:54:46,283
Go ahead.

1598
00:54:46,283 --> 00:54:47,784
Hey, I'm tougher than you.

1599
00:54:47,784 --> 00:54:49,185
- [Crow] Hey, I could get
about a buck for this.

1600
00:54:49,185 --> 00:54:50,420
I'm keeping it.

1601
00:54:50,420 --> 00:54:51,354
- [Servo] I wonder if
they're good eating.

1602
00:54:51,354 --> 00:54:53,690
You could boil them in beer.

1603
00:54:53,690 --> 00:54:55,725
- [Joel] Come back, we
have yet to taunt you.

1604
00:54:55,725 --> 00:54:57,761
We are the planet
of novelty items.

1605
00:54:59,229 --> 00:55:00,964
- Stand by.
- Deceleration rockets.

1606
00:55:01,931 --> 00:55:03,933
- Thrust, 18, 21.

1607
00:55:03,933 --> 00:55:06,736
24.
- 42, hut, hut.

1608
00:55:06,736 --> 00:55:07,904
Hike, go long.

1609
00:55:10,740 --> 00:55:13,243
- [Servo] It's Roger Ramjet
and his American eagles.

1610
00:55:14,210 --> 00:55:16,212
Take their proton pills.

1611
00:55:19,582 --> 00:55:21,818
- Hey hey, I'm down here.

1612
00:55:21,818 --> 00:55:23,019
(mock coughing)

1613
00:55:23,019 --> 00:55:24,321
Hey.

1614
00:55:24,321 --> 00:55:25,588
- [Joel] I'm glad you're back.

1615
00:55:25,588 --> 00:55:26,823
We make excellent
stocking stuffers.

1616
00:55:26,823 --> 00:55:28,191
You will come to
know that in time.

1617
00:55:29,359 --> 00:55:30,293
- [Servo] I know
how to cheer him up.

1618
00:55:30,293 --> 00:55:31,961
Tickle machine, tickle machine.

1619
00:55:31,961 --> 00:55:33,063
- Get him, get him.

1620
00:55:33,063 --> 00:55:35,732
(mock laughter)

1621
00:55:42,138 --> 00:55:43,073
Lock it.

1622
00:55:43,073 --> 00:55:44,974
Looks like a bad neighborhood.

1623
00:55:44,974 --> 00:55:46,810
- [Joel] Plaster doggy doo?

1624
00:55:46,810 --> 00:55:47,644
Rubber vomit?

1625
00:55:47,644 --> 00:55:48,845
What is this?

1626
00:55:51,348 --> 00:55:53,550
- Planet of Johnson Smith.

1627
00:55:55,585 --> 00:55:58,788
- [Servo] Hey, these prices
are quite reasonable.

1628
00:55:58,788 --> 00:56:00,590
- His crawl-o-copter exploded.

1629
00:56:00,590 --> 00:56:01,758
Poor old Brinkmann.

1630
00:56:02,926 --> 00:56:04,294
- There's the cause.

1631
00:56:04,294 --> 00:56:05,995
There's a high tension
line underground.

1632
00:56:05,995 --> 00:56:07,997
Durand, get the
crawlers out of the way

1633
00:56:07,997 --> 00:56:09,366
or the next time
the voltage mounts,

1634
00:56:09,366 --> 00:56:11,401
exactly the same thing
will happen to us.

1635
00:56:12,569 --> 00:56:14,671
- [Joel] Oh it just
looks like a big fish.

1636
00:56:17,640 --> 00:56:20,043
- Mommy, Daddy, I am home.

1637
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:22,245
- [Joel] Oh, you
wonderful, fun-derful

1638
00:56:22,245 --> 00:56:23,613
spunky little robot.

1639
00:56:23,613 --> 00:56:26,282
(mock kissing noise)

1640
00:56:26,282 --> 00:56:27,117
- Omigow.

1641
00:56:27,117 --> 00:56:27,951
- [Servo] Oh my god?

1642
00:56:27,951 --> 00:56:29,719
Did he say oh my god?

1643
00:56:31,154 --> 00:56:33,156
- Brinkmann, we
thought you were dead.

1644
00:56:33,156 --> 00:56:34,557
- [Joel] I am filled with life.

1645
00:56:34,557 --> 00:56:36,159
Get to know me, friends.

1646
00:56:36,159 --> 00:56:37,794
- Why, what do you mean?

1647
00:56:37,794 --> 00:56:39,129
- There's a high
tension line over there.

1648
00:56:39,129 --> 00:56:40,163
- [Servo] Oh, what do you know?

1649
00:56:40,163 --> 00:56:41,364
- Now, your machine blew up

1650
00:56:41,364 --> 00:56:42,532
just because you landed right

1651
00:56:42,532 --> 00:56:44,167
on top of that
surface power line.

1652
00:56:44,167 --> 00:56:45,368
- [Joel] Oh, that's rich.

1653
00:56:45,368 --> 00:56:46,870
- All we have to
do was to follow it

1654
00:56:46,870 --> 00:56:48,738
and it will probably leads us
to the inhabitants of Venus.

1655
00:56:48,738 --> 00:56:49,939
- Oh you kill me.
- Or not.

1656
00:56:49,939 --> 00:56:51,941
- There's no point
in trying to do that.

1657
00:56:51,941 --> 00:56:54,043
I've already found the
inhabitants of Venus

1658
00:56:54,043 --> 00:56:56,780
and I've brought one
of them back for you.

1659
00:56:59,048 --> 00:56:59,883
- [Servo] Yeah, they're on sale.

1660
00:56:59,883 --> 00:57:00,984
Really reasonable, too.

1661
00:57:01,951 --> 00:57:02,852
- What is it?

1662
00:57:02,852 --> 00:57:03,987
- [Joel] It's art.

1663
00:57:03,987 --> 00:57:05,488
You bring your
preconceptions to it.

1664
00:57:05,488 --> 00:57:06,823
- I wonder if it
is a form of life.

1665
00:57:08,291 --> 00:57:10,693
- Great, he put another
life form in his pocket.

1666
00:57:11,661 --> 00:57:13,530
- All right, T'Chen Yu.

1667
00:57:13,530 --> 00:57:14,431
- [Servo] Why are
you still here?

1668
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:15,665
Beat it.

1669
00:57:15,665 --> 00:57:17,066
- Let's go and try
to follow that line.

1670
00:57:17,066 --> 00:57:18,001
- Okay.

1671
00:57:18,001 --> 00:57:19,035
- Still feel stupid?

1672
00:57:21,471 --> 00:57:24,641
(mock engine revving)

1673
00:57:29,179 --> 00:57:31,281
- Omigow, come on.

1674
00:57:31,281 --> 00:57:32,248
- [Servo] Kam-I-ken?

1675
00:57:32,248 --> 00:57:34,284
- [Joel] Yeah yeah, here I come.

1676
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:35,552
bidi bidi, beats all.

1677
00:57:35,552 --> 00:57:37,754
That's the way these
clowns order me around.

1678
00:57:41,157 --> 00:57:42,625
- Crawler, please come in.

1679
00:57:42,625 --> 00:57:44,027
Crawler, please come in.

1680
00:57:44,027 --> 00:57:45,228
- [Servo] Grab it.

1681
00:57:45,228 --> 00:57:46,362
- [Crow] Would you
like fries with that?

1682
00:57:47,530 --> 00:57:49,065
- There's something
very strange here.

1683
00:57:49,065 --> 00:57:52,402
A white sphere that looks
like an immense golf ball.

1684
00:57:52,402 --> 00:57:54,871
- [Servo] I think
he meant goofball.

1685
00:57:54,871 --> 00:57:56,172
- and it's teed up.

1686
00:57:57,740 --> 00:57:59,576
Looks like a Schlesinger Nine.

1687
00:57:59,576 --> 00:58:01,544
What a hell of a line.

1688
00:58:01,544 --> 00:58:02,946
- It's incredible.

1689
00:58:02,946 --> 00:58:04,948
You think it's a
machine, Orloff?

1690
00:58:04,948 --> 00:58:06,382
- Well, I can't say yet.

1691
00:58:07,517 --> 00:58:08,651
I don't know.

1692
00:58:08,651 --> 00:58:10,286
Everything here is so strange.

1693
00:58:10,286 --> 00:58:12,355
- [Joel] Why do they
have a bent coat hanger

1694
00:58:12,355 --> 00:58:15,024
around their mirror,
is that foreshadowing?

1695
00:58:15,024 --> 00:58:17,260
(laughing)

1696
00:58:19,462 --> 00:58:21,197
- Then, perhaps,
we'll understand.

1697
00:58:21,197 --> 00:58:22,699
- [Joel] You know, we've
become fast friends.

1698
00:58:22,699 --> 00:58:25,068
- Let me know when you've
got your instruments ready.

1699
00:58:25,068 --> 00:58:26,402
Now, I'll need all
the figures I can get.

1700
00:58:26,402 --> 00:58:28,071
- [Servo] Bugles, trombones.

1701
00:58:28,071 --> 00:58:29,339
- Good.

1702
00:58:29,339 --> 00:58:30,507
- I knew he'd say that.

1703
00:58:30,507 --> 00:58:32,208
- Talua, stay in
first contact with us.

1704
00:58:32,208 --> 00:58:33,376
- Very well, professor.

1705
00:58:33,376 --> 00:58:36,079
(tense music)

1706
00:58:36,079 --> 00:58:38,381
- I am looking at Venus
on the observation screen

1707
00:58:38,381 --> 00:58:40,049
at the Cosmostraiter.

1708
00:58:40,049 --> 00:58:42,018
Everything is strangely quiet.

1709
00:58:42,018 --> 00:58:44,320
Is this the calm
before the storm?

1710
00:58:44,320 --> 00:58:46,389
Why don't the Venusian's answer?

1711
00:58:46,389 --> 00:58:47,991
- [Servo] Why do I talk
into my toothbrush?

1712
00:58:47,991 --> 00:58:49,492
- Are these metallic
insects really the masters

1713
00:58:49,492 --> 00:58:50,493
of this planet?

1714
00:58:50,493 --> 00:58:51,628
- Ah, who cares?

1715
00:58:51,628 --> 00:58:53,429
- T'Chen Yu is
working day and night

1716
00:58:53,429 --> 00:58:55,965
to solve the mystery of
these strange creatures.

1717
00:58:57,200 --> 00:59:00,270
- Tonight, big sale at
Bill Fiber Oldstown.

1718
00:59:00,270 --> 00:59:01,804
We've got hot dogs for
the kids and suckers.

1719
00:59:01,804 --> 00:59:02,906
Speaking of suckers, look
at this sucker over here.

1720
00:59:02,906 --> 00:59:03,740
A 1928 porter.

1721
00:59:03,740 --> 00:59:05,074
Hey, come on down.

1722
00:59:08,244 --> 00:59:09,979
- [Joel] What a day, huh?

1723
00:59:09,979 --> 00:59:11,748
- [Servo] Hey, how are
the sea monkeys coming?

1724
00:59:14,450 --> 00:59:16,386
- [Joel] Hey, give me
a crack at that, huh?

1725
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:17,921
Come on.

1726
00:59:17,921 --> 00:59:20,723
- We have investigated
your strange inhabitants.

1727
00:59:20,723 --> 00:59:22,025
They're completely harmless.

1728
00:59:22,025 --> 00:59:23,459
They're not a form of life.

1729
00:59:23,459 --> 00:59:25,795
- Well now think how
scared I was in that hole.

1730
00:59:25,795 --> 00:59:28,898
- Your discovery is more
significant than you think.

1731
00:59:28,898 --> 00:59:31,834
I put one of the
microcrystal in the marrocks.

1732
00:59:31,834 --> 00:59:32,969
Listen.

1733
00:59:32,969 --> 00:59:37,340
(ethereal electronic whirring)

1734
00:59:37,340 --> 00:59:39,475
- [Servo] Oh yeah, that's
really significant.

1735
00:59:39,475 --> 00:59:42,045
- Can't you get the
station in clearer?

1736
00:59:42,045 --> 00:59:44,914
Don't you have a convertor
box or some tin foil

1737
00:59:44,914 --> 00:59:46,015
to put on the antenna?

1738
00:59:48,818 --> 00:59:50,219
- [Servo] Rabbit
ears might do it.

1739
00:59:54,290 --> 00:59:55,959
- [Joel] Oh, that's sad.

1740
00:59:58,761 --> 00:59:59,596
- [Servo] So.

1741
00:59:59,596 --> 01:00:00,797
- Yes.

1742
01:00:00,797 --> 01:00:03,533
Those were the voices
of the Venusians.

1743
01:00:03,533 --> 01:00:06,269
I would say that these
strange metallic insects

1744
01:00:06,269 --> 01:00:08,771
had a way of storing
sound effects.

1745
01:00:08,771 --> 01:00:10,239
- [Joel] Groovy.

1746
01:00:10,239 --> 01:00:11,574
- Are you trying to tell us

1747
01:00:11,574 --> 01:00:14,110
that the Venusian's
used these insects

1748
01:00:14,110 --> 01:00:15,645
to record both speech and sound?

1749
01:00:15,645 --> 01:00:16,512
- That's right.

1750
01:00:16,512 --> 01:00:17,747
- But that's fantastic.

1751
01:00:17,747 --> 01:00:19,015
- [Servo] Thanks,
like you'd know.

1752
01:00:19,015 --> 01:00:20,817
- Well that would
mean that the hole

1753
01:00:20,817 --> 01:00:22,552
which Brinkmann fell into,

1754
01:00:22,552 --> 01:00:24,087
is a chamber of archives.

1755
01:00:24,087 --> 01:00:27,256
- [Crow] Oh right, and
they were all librarians.

1756
01:00:27,256 --> 01:00:28,625
- Of this planet.

1757
01:00:28,625 --> 01:00:31,260
- But then where could
the inhabitants be?

1758
01:00:31,260 --> 01:00:32,862
He certainly saw
a spaceship land.

1759
01:00:32,862 --> 01:00:33,696
He couldn't of missed it.

1760
01:00:33,696 --> 01:00:35,131
Yet, nothing happened.

1761
01:00:35,131 --> 01:00:36,299
- [Servo] Oh, maybe
there was a ball game on.

1762
01:00:36,299 --> 01:00:37,533
- Nothing at all.

1763
01:00:37,533 --> 01:00:38,801
- And my machine blowing up.

1764
01:00:38,801 --> 01:00:40,269
You call that nothing?

1765
01:00:40,269 --> 01:00:41,638
- [Servo] Yeah.

1766
01:00:41,638 --> 01:00:43,106
- I need more figures.

1767
01:00:43,106 --> 01:00:44,307
- We had figures.

1768
01:00:44,307 --> 01:00:45,708
Strange figures.

1769
01:00:45,708 --> 01:00:47,343
- More of those
metallic insects.

1770
01:00:51,214 --> 01:00:52,548
- [Servo] Forceps.

1771
01:00:52,548 --> 01:00:53,516
- [Narrator] The
research program

1772
01:00:53,516 --> 01:00:55,284
was going according to plan.

1773
01:00:55,284 --> 01:00:57,854
We are all fascinated
by the petrified forest.

1774
01:00:57,854 --> 01:00:59,022
- [Joel] And it likes us, too.

1775
01:00:59,022 --> 01:01:00,256
- [Narrator] Our
spacesuits are so heavy

1776
01:01:00,256 --> 01:01:02,125
that working outside
the ship is difficult.

1777
01:01:03,393 --> 01:01:04,694
The investigation
of the power lines

1778
01:01:04,694 --> 01:01:06,129
leading to the white sphere

1779
01:01:06,129 --> 01:01:08,398
and measurement
attention changes

1780
01:01:08,398 --> 01:01:10,066
is down by a silo craft.

1781
01:01:10,066 --> 01:01:11,768
The storms, which
whip across Venus,

1782
01:01:11,768 --> 01:01:13,069
only make the work harder.

1783
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,873
- You know, these winds
only make the work harder.

1784
01:01:16,873 --> 01:01:18,941
- That's where the lines
lead to, all right.

1785
01:01:21,244 --> 01:01:22,078
There's no doubt.

1786
01:01:22,078 --> 01:01:22,912
- [Servo] Yeah, I know.

1787
01:01:22,912 --> 01:01:24,180
I was a meter man, once.

1788
01:01:25,748 --> 01:01:26,816
- That's it.

1789
01:01:26,816 --> 01:01:28,584
- [Servo] Yup.

1790
01:01:28,584 --> 01:01:29,485
That's the ticket.

1791
01:01:34,057 --> 01:01:36,926
- [Narrator] T'Chen was
collecting samples of the sand

