pounds of doodie,

2047
01:12:02,217 --> 01:12:03,552
is what it was.

2048
01:12:03,552 --> 01:12:04,453
- Where are the others?

2049
01:12:04,453 --> 01:12:05,888
I can't see them.

2050
01:12:07,056 --> 01:12:09,558
- Bidi-bidi-bidi.
- Spunky, come back.

2051
01:12:09,558 --> 01:12:11,060
Come back, Spunky.

2052
01:12:13,829 --> 01:12:15,731
- Well, that scene
was a load of crap.

2053
01:12:21,437 --> 01:12:24,940
- [Servo] Beware the
turd of Altair Seven.

2054
01:12:24,940 --> 01:12:27,209
- [Joel] Spotlight dance.

2055
01:12:27,209 --> 01:12:28,711
- I see what Durand meant now.

2056
01:12:28,711 --> 01:12:30,946
It's a model they
use to work out

2057
01:12:30,946 --> 01:12:33,048
their plans of
attack on the Earth.

2058
01:12:33,048 --> 01:12:34,850
- Good thing the Venusians
can never get far away

2059
01:12:34,850 --> 01:12:36,051
from the bathroom.

2060
01:12:36,051 --> 01:12:37,653
- It said they would
first subject the planet

2061
01:12:37,653 --> 01:12:40,356
to a highly intense
radiation bombardment.

2062
01:12:40,356 --> 01:12:42,524
Thanks to this device,
they calculated

2063
01:12:42,524 --> 01:12:43,525
how atomic beams

2064
01:12:43,525 --> 01:12:45,894
could be directed to our planet.

2065
01:12:45,894 --> 01:12:47,363
- I think you are quite right

2066
01:12:47,363 --> 01:12:48,497
and directly beneath us

2067
01:12:48,497 --> 01:12:50,366
is their operation headquarters.

2068
01:12:50,366 --> 01:12:51,533
- [Servo] Neat.

2069
01:12:51,533 --> 01:12:53,035
There it is.

2070
01:12:53,035 --> 01:12:55,571
- [Joel] Oh, there's
joy in kookville.

2071
01:12:56,905 --> 01:12:59,274
- [Servo] Speaking
of joy, let's blow.

2072
01:12:59,274 --> 01:13:00,576
- The magic toothbrush
wills save them.

2073
01:13:00,576 --> 01:13:01,410
Go, toughy, go.

2074
01:13:07,349 --> 01:13:10,119
(doors whirring)

2075
01:13:18,093 --> 01:13:22,131
- And we'll be right
back after this message.

2076
01:13:22,131 --> 01:13:24,700
Hi, Ed Herlihy here
hoping you're enjoying

2077
01:13:24,700 --> 01:13:26,969
tonight's Klack festival
theater presentation

2078
01:13:26,969 --> 01:13:28,670
of First Spaceship to Venus.

2079
01:13:28,670 --> 01:13:30,873
You know, holiday season
is the perfect time

2080
01:13:30,873 --> 01:13:33,275
to enjoy Klack's
industrial salad based

2081
01:13:33,275 --> 01:13:36,211
snacks and snippets
anytime of the day or year.

2082
01:13:36,211 --> 01:13:38,046
Start the morning with
a technicolor yawn

2083
01:13:38,046 --> 01:13:40,949
by serving up piles of
flabby Klack leather pancakes

2084
01:13:40,949 --> 01:13:42,985
dotted with dicey coco stunks.

2085
01:13:42,985 --> 01:13:44,319
Kids can't resist the texture

2086
01:13:44,319 --> 01:13:46,588
of Klack's creamy
clotted palm spread,

2087
01:13:46,588 --> 01:13:47,823
squeezed out on horsey biscuits

2088
01:13:47,823 --> 01:13:50,459
and don't forget the
Sir Cheddar snack a lots

2089
01:13:50,459 --> 01:13:51,660
and top them with Jimmy Hats

2090
01:13:51,660 --> 01:13:54,196
for a western roundup
and safe snacking.

2091
01:13:54,196 --> 01:13:56,732
And Moms, don't forget
to serve the claver club

2092
01:13:56,732 --> 01:13:58,700
platters of salamander
finger-wiches,

2093
01:13:58,700 --> 01:13:59,968
creamy crust puppies,

2094
01:13:59,968 --> 01:14:01,904
and hey, try a load
of taco minced meat

2095
01:14:01,904 --> 01:14:03,939
relish parfait served
up in a tulip glass

2096
01:14:03,939 --> 01:14:05,641
for that touch of elegance.

2097
01:14:05,641 --> 01:14:07,342
Uncle Bob's just out
of the institution.

2098
01:14:07,342 --> 01:14:09,111
Celebrate with skin mittens.

2099
01:14:09,111 --> 01:14:11,613
Brightened up with gamey
forest meat stuffing

2100
01:14:11,613 --> 01:14:13,916
and don't forget those
Polynesian cheese devils.

2101
01:14:13,916 --> 01:14:17,286
Then, pinch off some Klack
hanger crafted cobra coils

2102
01:14:17,286 --> 01:14:19,321
to compliment a
Bastille day buffet

2103
01:14:19,321 --> 01:14:20,823
and lube up those cooter cakes

2104
01:14:20,823 --> 01:14:23,225
with that incredibly
edible, spreadable phlegm.

2105
01:14:23,225 --> 01:14:25,627
Watch kitty's
galvanic skin response

2106
01:14:25,627 --> 01:14:26,562
shoot through the ceiling

2107
01:14:26,562 --> 01:14:27,930
by wrapping him in Klack wrap

2108
01:14:27,930 --> 01:14:29,998
and making her a
festive centerpiece.

2109
01:14:29,998 --> 01:14:32,501
At lunch time, light
your hand on fire

2110
01:14:32,501 --> 01:14:35,237
and plunge it into
the traditional gut
loaf whistle pie.

2111
01:14:35,237 --> 01:14:37,840
Just like grandpa used to do
before they took him away.

2112
01:14:37,840 --> 01:14:41,210
And finally, dress your
holiday table in style

2113
01:14:41,210 --> 01:14:43,245
with a gold roasted
mutant hell beast.

2114
01:14:43,245 --> 01:14:45,147
Stuffed with flesh
button dressing.

2115
01:14:45,147 --> 01:14:46,949
Made fresh with Klack saladoos,

2116
01:14:46,949 --> 01:14:49,251
cooter croutons, and
grandmother's earlobes.

2117
01:14:49,251 --> 01:14:50,552
Always the best.

2118
01:14:50,552 --> 01:14:52,387
Accent with creamy
crust puppies,

2119
01:14:52,387 --> 01:14:53,622
velvety chode balls,

2120
01:14:53,622 --> 01:14:55,824
and of course, a mug
of holiday swill.

2121
01:14:55,824 --> 01:14:58,126
Remember, if you're
incapable of showing emotion

2122
01:14:58,126 --> 01:14:59,328
but know how to cook,

2123
01:14:59,328 --> 01:15:01,263
Klack has a snack idea for you.

2124
01:15:02,998 --> 01:15:06,935
And we'll be right back
after these messages.

2125
01:15:06,935 --> 01:15:09,505
(upbeat music)

2126
01:15:14,243 --> 01:15:15,611
- [Crow] If you'd
like to make a call.

2127
01:15:15,611 --> 01:15:17,012
Please hang up and call again.

2128
01:15:17,012 --> 01:15:18,080
- [Both] If you'd
like to make a call,

2129
01:15:18,080 --> 01:15:19,581
please hang up and call again.

2130
01:15:19,581 --> 01:15:21,517
- Sikarna, the glass
forest is radiating energy.

2131
01:15:21,517 --> 01:15:22,885
Come quickly.

2132
01:15:22,885 --> 01:15:25,621
(dramatic music)

2133
01:15:30,025 --> 01:15:31,660
- That's just what
I was afraid of.

2134
01:15:31,660 --> 01:15:32,528
- [Servo] Oh why
didn't you tell us,

2135
01:15:32,528 --> 01:15:34,062
mister know it all?

2136
01:15:34,062 --> 01:15:34,997
- Look at that.

2137
01:15:34,997 --> 01:15:35,964
- [Joel] Oh, it makes me sick.

2138
01:15:35,964 --> 01:15:37,232
- The sphere's turned red.

2139
01:15:37,232 --> 01:15:38,467
- Maybe it's embarrassed.

2140
01:15:40,202 --> 01:15:41,470
- I am not surprised.

2141
01:15:41,470 --> 01:15:42,704
- [All] Shut up!

2142
01:15:44,339 --> 01:15:45,440
- No.

2143
01:15:45,440 --> 01:15:46,708
Now everything is clear.

2144
01:15:46,708 --> 01:15:47,943
- [Servo] Yeah, sure.

2145
01:15:47,943 --> 01:15:49,745
- The sphere creates an
artificial force field

2146
01:15:49,745 --> 01:15:52,514
which strengthens
the gravitation.

2147
01:15:52,514 --> 01:15:53,348
- [Joel] Strengthens it?

2148
01:15:53,348 --> 01:15:54,550
- Diminishes it.

2149
01:15:54,550 --> 01:15:56,952
At this very moment,
the power is emanating.

2150
01:15:56,952 --> 01:15:57,886
- [Servo] Menting, yeah.

2151
01:15:57,886 --> 01:15:59,154
- When the energy is inverted,

2152
01:15:59,154 --> 01:16:01,223
the field will reverse itself.

2153
01:16:01,223 --> 01:16:02,624
- [Servo] Reserved, huh huh.

2154
01:16:02,624 --> 01:16:04,159
- We'll be hurled into space.

2155
01:16:04,159 --> 01:16:05,661
- Well, that's interesting but
does it belong in the script?

2156
01:16:05,661 --> 01:16:06,828
- There's still time.

2157
01:16:06,828 --> 01:16:07,763
- [Servo] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2158
01:16:07,763 --> 01:16:11,533
If you build it, he will come.

2159
01:16:11,533 --> 01:16:13,068
- Hello, Harringway,
come in, please.

2160
01:16:13,068 --> 01:16:14,236
- Joel, what's a herring weigh?

2161
01:16:14,236 --> 01:16:15,070
- [Joel] About a pound.

2162
01:16:15,070 --> 01:16:16,204
(laughing)

2163
01:16:16,204 --> 01:16:17,406
- Threes the charm.

2164
01:16:17,406 --> 01:16:19,107
- [Servo] This is
where I want to live.

2165
01:16:19,107 --> 01:16:20,842
The weather's so great.

2166
01:16:20,842 --> 01:16:24,012
(soft dramatic music)

2167
01:16:31,653 --> 01:16:33,488
- Geeze, I hope
this baby starts.

2168
01:16:33,488 --> 01:16:36,592
I think I left
the dome light on.

2169
01:16:36,592 --> 01:16:38,026
- [Joel] Just throw
that stuff anywhere.

2170
01:16:38,026 --> 01:16:39,394
I kinda live out of my car.

2171
01:16:40,896 --> 01:16:43,532
(mock engine revving)

2172
01:16:43,532 --> 01:16:44,967
Get into these metal cars.

2173
01:16:44,967 --> 01:16:47,035
We'll be safe from
the lightning here.

2174
01:16:48,203 --> 01:16:49,838
- [Servo] In the future,
they drive AMC Pacers.

2175
01:16:49,838 --> 01:16:51,573
- I'm getting car sick.

2176
01:16:51,573 --> 01:16:53,075
- [Joel] Okay, who knows a song?

2177
01:16:53,075 --> 01:16:54,476
Come on, let's have fun.

2178
01:16:55,711 --> 01:16:56,578
- [Servo] I know.

2179
01:16:57,980 --> 01:16:58,814
- Oh hey.

2180
01:17:01,216 --> 01:17:02,117
- They're shadows.

2181
01:17:03,285 --> 01:17:05,053
- Thrown on the wall
when they were hit

2182
01:17:05,053 --> 01:17:06,588
by an atomic explosion.

2183
01:17:06,588 --> 01:17:07,956
- [Servo] So they all look
like Tina Turner, I guess.

2184
01:17:07,956 --> 01:17:10,025
- Incredible.
- Those crummy vandals.

2185
01:17:10,025 --> 01:17:12,094
Can't leave anything alone.

2186
01:17:12,094 --> 01:17:13,695
- And now the only thing
that is left of them

2187
01:17:13,695 --> 01:17:15,464
is their shadows.

2188
01:17:15,464 --> 01:17:16,965
(mock snoring)

2189
01:17:16,965 --> 01:17:18,867
- [Servo] Oh, I thought you
were gonna say something else.

2190
01:17:18,867 --> 01:17:20,369
- Goodnight and may god bless.

2191
01:17:23,205 --> 01:17:25,374
- The maddocks is
picking up commands

2192
01:17:25,374 --> 01:17:26,975
from the underground
nerve center.

2193
01:17:26,975 --> 01:17:28,243
- [Joel] I knew that.

2194
01:17:28,243 --> 01:17:30,278
- Look at the key it's
using to decode them.

2195
01:17:30,278 --> 01:17:33,015
- Why it's, it's
incredible, Sikarna.

2196
01:17:33,015 --> 01:17:34,016
- [Servo] Thank you.

2197
01:17:35,183 --> 01:17:36,685
- E=MC2.

2198
01:17:36,685 --> 01:17:37,819
- [Joel] I stole that.

2199
01:17:37,819 --> 01:17:40,022
- That's Albert
Einstein's old formula.

2200
01:17:40,022 --> 01:17:41,289
- Yes but their
intergradation factor

2201
01:17:41,289 --> 01:17:43,792
is a curved closed upon its own.

2202
01:17:43,792 --> 01:17:46,561
- [Servo] Wow, pretty neat.

2203
01:17:46,561 --> 01:17:48,263
- Hey come here, you
gotta check this out.

2204
01:17:48,263 --> 01:17:49,364
Look at this.

2205
01:17:50,799 --> 01:17:52,467
- Take a look, it's interesting.

2206
01:17:52,467 --> 01:17:53,869
- [Joel] Well, that's first.

2207
01:17:55,404 --> 01:17:57,739
- [Servo] Oh, that's disgusting.

2208
01:17:59,441 --> 01:18:00,375
Neat, though.

2209
01:18:00,375 --> 01:18:01,476
- That's wonderful.

2210
01:18:01,476 --> 01:18:02,310
Those are seeds.

2211
01:18:02,310 --> 01:18:03,578
- I know, they're mine.

2212
01:18:03,578 --> 01:18:04,646
- They're plant seeds.

2213
01:18:04,646 --> 01:18:05,580
- Yeah.

2214
01:18:05,580 --> 01:18:06,982
- Where did you find them?

2215
01:18:06,982 --> 01:18:09,184
- I found them on the surface,
near the nerve center.

2216
01:18:09,184 --> 01:18:10,318
- [Servo] Spilled them.

2217
01:18:10,318 --> 01:18:11,720
- They were certainly
carried there

2218
01:18:11,720 --> 01:18:13,021
by one of those big storms

2219
01:18:13,021 --> 01:18:15,123
and if these seeds
are still fertile,

2220
01:18:15,123 --> 01:18:17,092
it proves there is
life on this planet.

2221
01:18:19,194 --> 01:18:20,395
- [Intercom] Professor Sikarna

2222
01:18:20,395 --> 01:18:21,763
wants everybody in
the maddocks, please.

2223
01:18:21,763 --> 01:18:23,999
- [Joel] Oh, that's just
great, we're busted.

2224
01:18:25,967 --> 01:18:28,570
- I knew you were
going to cut to me.

2225
01:18:29,971 --> 01:18:32,574
- Our researches on the metal
insects found in the cave

2226
01:18:32,574 --> 01:18:35,343
have told us so little
of this planet's history.

2227
01:18:35,343 --> 01:18:39,247
As to the message we heard,
there's no doubt about it.

2228
01:18:39,247 --> 01:18:40,382
- [Joel] They said.

2229
01:18:40,382 --> 01:18:41,583
- [All] Run!

2230
01:18:41,583 --> 01:18:42,818
- The inhabitants of
Venus were contemplating

2231
01:18:42,818 --> 01:18:44,986
launching an atomic
attack on our planet.

2232
01:18:46,521 --> 01:18:48,156
Now the attack
wasn't carried out.

2233
01:18:48,156 --> 01:18:49,658
- Good for us.

2234
01:18:49,658 --> 01:18:51,993
- An accident they didn't
expect upset their plan.

2235
01:18:51,993 --> 01:18:53,462
- The A-Team.

2236
01:18:53,462 --> 01:18:55,697
- Their atomic weapons
got out of their control.

2237
01:18:55,697 --> 01:18:56,631
- [Servo] As did their bowels.

2238
01:18:56,631 --> 01:18:58,033
- Chain reaction was unleashed

2239
01:18:58,033 --> 01:18:59,901
and they all perished.

2240
01:18:59,901 --> 01:19:01,470
- Only their shadows remained.

2241
01:19:02,471 --> 01:19:03,839
- [Joel] I knew that.

2242
01:19:03,839 --> 01:19:06,141
- Energy projectors,
although partially destroyed,

2243
01:19:06,141 --> 01:19:07,576
are capable of working again.

2244
01:19:07,576 --> 01:19:10,378
If their energy reactions
are set in motion by

2245
01:19:10,378 --> 01:19:12,547
some accident or
even by one of us.

2246
01:19:12,547 --> 01:19:15,517
- Why, what do you mean?

2247
01:19:15,517 --> 01:19:17,619
That we've started the reaction?

2248
01:19:17,619 --> 01:19:18,887
- No, baldy did.

2249
01:19:20,288 --> 01:19:22,624
- When that rock fell
into the black mud,

2250
01:19:22,624 --> 01:19:23,458
what happened?

2251
01:19:23,458 --> 01:19:24,292
- Oh the rock.

2252
01:19:24,292 --> 01:19:25,527
Would you let that die?

2253
01:19:25,527 --> 01:19:27,062
- As if the slime
was a living thing.

2254
01:19:27,062 --> 01:19:28,930
- Then something
terrible happened.

2255
01:19:28,930 --> 01:19:30,866
The slime began to grow rapidly.

2256
01:19:30,866 --> 01:19:32,601
- Then it got its own series.

2257
01:19:32,601 --> 01:19:33,435
- Dilated.

2258
01:19:33,435 --> 01:19:34,636
Now tell him.

2259
01:19:34,636 --> 01:19:36,371
What happened next.

2260
01:19:36,371 --> 01:19:37,973
The black slime started to move.

2261
01:19:37,973 --> 01:19:40,842
- Yes, it began to follow us.

2262
01:19:40,842 --> 01:19:41,877
We were cornered.

2263
01:19:41,877 --> 01:19:42,811
- What did you do?

2264
01:19:42,811 --> 01:19:44,813
- I used the (mumbles) ray gun

2265
01:19:44,813 --> 01:19:46,348
and I shot into it.

2266
01:19:46,348 --> 01:19:47,883
- [Servo] Then we frightened
it away with a coat hanger.

2267
01:19:47,883 --> 01:19:50,118
- You should never
have done that.

2268
01:19:51,319 --> 01:19:52,988
You started an atomic reaction.

2269
01:19:52,988 --> 01:19:55,524
- [Joel] Oh, everybody's
dumping on me.

2270
01:19:55,524 --> 01:19:57,292
- We had no other
way of getting out.

2271
01:19:57,292 --> 01:19:58,627
- Yes.

2272
01:20:00,428 --> 01:20:02,664
You started a chain reaction.

2273
01:20:02,664 --> 01:20:04,633
Over the whole
atomic installation.

2274
01:20:04,633 --> 01:20:05,867
- Happy?

2275
01:20:05,867 --> 01:20:07,369
- Now we're really
in a nice place.

2276
01:20:07,369 --> 01:20:08,170
- [Servo] Yeah, now it's
really gonna hit the fan.

2277
01:20:08,170 --> 01:20:08,970
- What can we do?

2278
01:20:08,970 --> 01:20:09,938
- What time was it?

2279
01:20:09,938 --> 01:20:11,907
- 17 hours, 10.
- I remember.

2280
01:20:11,907 --> 01:20:12,741
- I knew that.

2281
01:20:12,741 --> 01:20:14,209
- Yes.

2282
01:20:14,209 --> 01:20:17,312
Yes, it was at that moment
the sphere turned red.

2283
01:20:18,480 --> 01:20:20,448
- It looks as if mass
changed into energy

2284
01:20:20,448 --> 01:20:24,085
by process rather like
that of the atom bomb.

2285
01:20:24,085 --> 01:20:25,554
- [Servo] I've written
a poem about it.

2286
01:20:25,554 --> 01:20:27,556
- The people of this planet
knew how to reverse the process.

2287
01:20:27,556 --> 01:20:29,457
They changed mass into energy

2288
01:20:29,457 --> 01:20:32,227
but also they could change
energy back into mass.

2289
01:20:32,227 --> 01:20:33,929
